  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "When Allegro considered buying the small financial-technology company FinAi, François Nuyts asked its cofounder Rafał Czernik to build a lending business inside the shopping platform. Czernik brought a team and technology that became the foundation of Allegro Pay. The service subsequently expanded to finance purchases for millions of customers.\n\nNuyts also treated delivery as part of winning repeat business. He examined software and bottlenecks affecting both the marketplace and its logistics partners. For merchants unwilling to build their own delivery systems, he proposed that Allegro provide them, aiming to make orders cheaper and more convenient for customers.",
    "html": "<p>When Allegro considered buying the small financial-technology company FinAi, François Nuyts asked its cofounder Rafał Czernik to build a lending business inside the shopping platform. Czernik brought a team and technology that became the foundation of Allegro Pay. The service subsequently expanded to finance purchases for millions of customers.</p>\r\n<p>Nuyts also treated delivery as part of winning repeat business. He examined software and bottlenecks affecting both the marketplace and its logistics partners. For merchants unwilling to build their own delivery systems, he proposed that Allegro provide them, aiming to make orders cheaper and more convenient for customers.</p>\r\n",
